  "scientific_review": [
    "Ten predeclared Kuroshio regional cases join2024-01-15/07-15 and18.5/21.5/24.5/27.5/29.5N. Each exact retained Wang model-axis case at nominal0.49m/14km tangent half-window resolves query geometry. Source case ID, report pointer, actual gate and tangent positions/statuses remain retained; lateral boundary-span failure is separately typed and does not itself reject a supported axis tangent.",
    "The axis source is a dated GLORYS12V1-derived regional geometry, not an independently observed axis. HYCOM00Z instantaneous velocities and daily source-axis geometry are not simultaneous observations or statistically independent confirmation; both assimilating model systems can share inputs. No retained Wang lateral boundary is used as a physical width, nor is its30percent criterion equated to this vertical component diagnostic.",
    "At each gate five fixed normal offsets(-40,-20,0,20,40km) sample nearest HYCOM model nodes within8km. The primary selector chooses the greatest positive10cm/s qualifying0–200m signed downstream component core, retaining first-offset tie order. Three selected maxima hit an outer offset(18.5N both dates;24.5N January). They remain edge_maximum_axis_unresolved; no search expansion or forced interior result.",
    "Full40-level0–5000m east/north and signed projected velocities remain at all50 sampled profiles, with actual source indices, nearest-node distances, source lead time, global/variable metadata and canonical decoded-profile hashes. A fixed reference bearing from the near-surface source-axis tangent remains locked through depth; deep opposite flow is not made positive by depth-by-depth rotation.",
    "The primary10cm/s lower contour resolves at9of10 selected nodes;July24.5N is censored before missing/dry support after300m. Paired connected threshold layers resolve at9nodes for5cm/s,9for10cm/s,10for20cm/s. Alternate contours retain the same selected horizontal node and own core/upper/lower diagnoses. These are threshold sensitivity cases, not physical bottoms, depth confidence intervals or full-current thickness.",
    "At interior27.5N and29.5N nodes primary10cm/s lower depths are486.9014955291585/507.29965327042805m inJanuary and722.017127422757/839.1689339151822m inJuly. These are local dated model-component depths, not annual minima/maxima, climatology, an observed seasonal range or a uniform route profile. Regional upstream18.5–29.5N scope does not inherit to Kuroshio Extension.",
    "The connected layer uses a surface0m upper boundary only where the native0m model sample connects continuously to its qualifying core; unsampled/missing depth breaks cannot be bridged. Censored domain/deep levels and bathymetry are never substituted as flow boundaries. Resolved selected threshold spans remain model descriptors even where both endpoints exist.",
    "Actual source retrieval used35720velocity-cell pairs and285760decoded array bytes, under fixed20000pairs-per-patch/250000cumulative and7MB decoded-array caps. Both component dimensions, units, instantaneous field declaration, standard positive-down metre depth axis and exact timestamps were checked. Coordinate axes were read first and velocity requests budgeted before retrieval. NetCDF-client wire bytes and original source-wire hashes are not instrumented or claimed.",
    "Twenty-nine cloud tests cover frozen lower contours/transport/paired layer behavior plus exact date/level/window/gate lookup, duplicate/missing/identity/depth rejection, retained unresolved axis/tangent cases, fixed tie/edge policy, signed counterflow, same-node alternate contours, missing-level censoring, null no-current selection and global/cumulative query-budget rejection. After actual retrieval, a separate retained-output audit reproduced diagnoses, hashes, time keys and physical eligibility in cloud.",
    "Code/operator metadata preparation and exact artifact retention were local on one idle CPU. All ocean-field retrieval, axis-case numerical use, contour/layer calculations and tests ran only in cloud. Existing canonical701 scoped references, source reviews and102 eddy-size references are preserved. No local browser/server/runtime/WASM or numerical ocean-field test was run.",
    "Official HYCOM source documentation was freshly accessed and confirms instantaneous standard-level model output, assimilation, archived date range ending2024-09-04 and public release terms. New access to the Nature source article and Figshare metadata via browsing failed; this work uses the already retained byte-pinned scientific axis report and existing protocol rather than claiming a new article/figure review.",
    "No canonical physical depth admission, whole-current route depth profile, width/depth volume join, cross-sectional area, volume, physical state passage or annual envelope is established. Next steps are source-compatible along-reference projection with gaps/edge flags preserved and broader temporal/axis checks, followed by separately typed inventory integration."
  ],
